    {
      "id": "p0152-b009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Before Toby insisted that this phone call remain entirely in English, the localization team assumed - like many other fans - that \"G\" referred to this secretive Gaster character. As such, early drafts of the Japanese translation had this line say \"Hello? May I speak to Ga--\" in English, but written using Japanese pronunciation.",
        "raw": "Before Toby insisted that this phone\ncall remain entirely in English, the\nlocalization team assumed - like\nmany other fans - that \"G\" referred\nto this secretive Gaster character. As\nsuch, early drafts of the Japanese\ntranslation had this line say \"Hello?\nMay I speak to Ga--\" in English, but\nwritten using Japanese pronunciation.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.61300391,
          0.71942143,
          0.91161535,
          0.87835714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.61167347,
          0.71870714,
          0.91294579,
          0.87942857
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          38,
          43,
          46,
          48,
          50,
          52,
          55,
          56,
          57
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "在 Toby 坚持这通电话必须完全保留英文之前，本地化团队和许多粉丝一样，以为“G”指的是神秘的 Gaster。因此，早期日文译稿写的是英语“Hello? May I speak to Ga—”（你好？请问 Ga——在吗），但用日语假名标出英语发音。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
